    ctaCopy: "Plan our family trip",
    intro: "We've sent 240+ families to Kenya. We know the camps where the kids get their own game drive vehicle. We know the lodge with a pool and a doctor on call. We know the Watamu stretch where a seven-year-old can snorkel safely. And we know what breaks when it goes wrong — which is the thing we prevent.",
    why: "Family travel in Kenya works because the country genuinely welcomes kids — and because we've done the logistics properly so the parents can be present. We map the nap windows, locate the pools, brief the camps, and make sure the pediatrician number is in your phone before you land.",
